AI DEVELOPMENT LOG
Helpdesk Ticket System

Purpose
-------
This file records the useful project-development conversation and decisions. It keeps the implementation history in one place and excludes unrelated discussion about moving between chats or improving prompts.

STAGE 1 - PROJECT SETUP
-----------------------
Request: Build a helpdesk ticket system.

The project was organized as:
- React and Vite frontend
- FastAPI backend
- SQLAlchemy database layer
- PostgreSQL database
- Docker Compose for the database

The frontend provides a dashboard and ticket creation form. The backend stores tickets and exposes API endpoints.

STAGE 2 - CORE TICKET FEATURES
------------------------------
Implemented ticket creation with:
- Customer name
- Ticket title
- Description
- Priority
- Response deadline
- Optional assignee

Implemented ticket listing with:
- Customer search
- Overdue filter
- Assignee filter
- Pagination
- Queue ordering

The queue puts overdue tickets first, then sorts by priority, response deadline, and creation time.

STAGE 3 - THE ESCALATION TWIST
------------------------------
Requirement:
Every automated run must find tickets that have breached their response deadline and increase priority by only one level.

Priority flow:
normal -> high -> urgent

Rules:
- Overdue normal tickets become high.
- Overdue high tickets become urgent.
- Urgent tickets remain urgent.
- A single run cannot skip a level.

The rule was placed in backend/app/escalation.py so that the automatic scheduler and manual API endpoint share the same logic.

The FastAPI lifespan starts a background check immediately and repeats it every 60 seconds. A manual endpoint was also added:
POST /tickets/escalate-overdue

STAGE 4 - FRONTEND WORK
-----------------------
The dashboard was improved with:
- Search and filter controls
- Pagination controls
- Priority and overdue badges
- Assignee display
- Response deadline indicators
- New Ticket modal
- High priority option
- Live queue indicator
- Manual Run check button
- Updated time indicator
- Escape-key modal closing
- Responsive layout
- Hover and loading states
- Navy, coral, amber, and green visual accents

The Vite development server proxies /api requests to the FastAPI server. This fixed the Codespaces problem where a browser opened through a forwarded URL could not reach its own localhost:8000.

STAGE 5 - PROBLEMS ENCOUNTERED
------------------------------
1. Wrong Python interpreter
The default Python environment did not contain FastAPI or Uvicorn. The project virtual environment did contain them.

Solution:
Use backend/venv/bin/python and select that interpreter in VS Code.

2. Docker Compose was started from the wrong directory
The compose file was inside helpdesk-ticket-system, not the repository root.

Solution:
Run docker compose from helpdesk-ticket-system.

3. Port conflicts
Port 5173 was already used by Vite and port 8000 was already used by Uvicorn.

Solution:
Reuse the running service or use another port, such as 5174 for the frontend.

4. Frontend API connection failure
The browser received Failed to fetch when the frontend called localhost:8000 through Codespaces.

Solution:
Use same-origin /api requests and configure the Vite proxy to forward them to 127.0.0.1:8000.

5. Testing escalation behavior
The time-based rule needed proof that only one level changed per run.

Solution:
Create an overdue normal ticket, run the check, confirm it becomes high, run the check again, and confirm it becomes urgent.

6. Screenshot capture limitation
The supplied screenshot was added to the repository as frontend/frontend.png and linked from README.md. Automated browser capture was attempted, but the container lacked the system library required by Chromium.

STAGE 6 - VALIDATION
--------------------
Successful checks included:
- API health request returned HTTP 200.
- Ticket creation returned HTTP 200.
- Created tickets persisted in PostgreSQL.
- Escalation changed normal to high on the first run.
- Escalation changed high to urgent on the next run.
- Frontend production build completed successfully.
- Backend compileall check completed successfully.
- README screenshot link was added and verified in the repository.

STAGE 7 - FINAL REPOSITORY
--------------------------
The completed project and documentation were pushed to the main branch.

Important documentation files:
- README.md: concise setup, stack, structure, API, UI, and escalation overview
- reasoning.md: short staged explanation of the implementation and solutions
- ai.log: this development history

Final result:
A persistent, responsive helpdesk queue with ticket creation, filtering, pagination, deadline visibility, automatic one-level escalation, Dockerized PostgreSQL, and a documented frontend screenshot.
